#: ../../../DirectX/SemanticSignatures.md:1
msgid "Semantic Signatures"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DirectX/SemanticSignatures.md:3
msgid "Overview"
msgstr "概覽"

#: ../../../DirectX/SemanticSignatures.md:5
msgid ""
"A semantic signature describes the inputs and outputs of an HLSL shader "
"entry point: the semantics each value carries, its component type, and where "
"it is placed in the input/output register space. The DirectX Container "
"(DXContainer) stores this information in binary signature parts (`ISG1`, "
"`OSG1`) and in the pipeline state validation part (`PSV0`). To assist with "
"the construction of, and interaction with, these parts, a semantic signature "
"is represented as metadata (`dx.semantic.signatures`) in the LLVM IR. The "
"metadata can then be converted to its binary form, as defined in "
"[SemanticSignatures.h]. This document serves as a reference for the metadata "
"representation of a semantic signature for users to interface with."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DirectX/SemanticSignatures.md:18
msgid "Metadata Representation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DirectX/SemanticSignatures.md:20
msgid ""
"Consider the reference shaders below, then the following sections describe "
"the metadata representation of their signatures and the corresponding "
"operands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DirectX/SemanticSignatures.md:44
msgid ""
"**Note:** A signature does not necessarily have a unique metadata "
"representation. Further, a malformed signature can be represented in the "
"metadata format, and so it is the user's responsibility to verify that it is "
"a well-formed signature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DirectX/SemanticSignatures.md:49
msgid "Named Signature Table"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DirectX/SemanticSignatures.md:55
msgid ""
"A named metadata node, `dx.semantic.signatures`, is used to identify the "
"table of per-entry-point semantic signatures. The table itself is a list of "
"references to function/signature triples. If no entry point has a signature, "
"the named metadata node may be omitted entirely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DirectX/SemanticSignatures.md:60
msgid "Function/Signature Triple"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DirectX/SemanticSignatures.md:66
msgid ""
"The function/signature triple associates an entry-point function (the first "
"operand) with its input signature element list (the second operand) and "
"output signature element list (the third operand). Either list may be "
"`null`. An entry function may appear at most once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DirectX/SemanticSignatures.md:71
msgid "Signature Element List"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DirectX/SemanticSignatures.md:77
msgid ""
"A signature element list consists of a list of references to signature "
"element nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DirectX/SemanticSignatures.md:80
msgid "Signature Element"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DirectX/SemanticSignatures.md:86
msgid ""
"A signature element describes a single packed range of signature rows. It "
"retains all information needed to serialize into `ISG1`, `OSG1` and `PSV0`."
msgstr ""

